## (c) Player wiring — thief_character.gd (edited span :997-1011)

- `_begin_wire_crank` (:989-995): gate unchanged (`can_act`,
  `equipped_tool == "zipwire"`, not grappling/mantling), sets
  `_is_cranking`, zeroes `_crank_elapsed` / `crank_progress`, calls
  `_play_wire_crank_clip`. Unchanged.
- `_play_wire_crank_clip` (:997-1011) — the one edited span. Before: two
  silent `return` no-ops (arms-off, `clip_name == ""`). After: same two
  returns, each logging first with the UE clip path, never crashing:
  - arms-off / null player / null lib ->
    `push_warning("ZipwireCrank: crank clip no-op without real arms
    (UE clip TAT/Content/Art/Animation/ThiefNisha/Anim/Zipwire/AN_ThiefNisha_Zipwire__Reload_Loop)")`
  - `ensure_fp_clip` returns `""` (manifest lacks the clip OR the
    `_retarget_general` zero-shared-bone path returned null, which already
    logs `shares no bones with skeleton; skipped (procedural fallback
    kept)` at animation_library.gd) ->
    `push_warning("ZipwireCrank: crank clip no-op, manifest lacks clip or
    zero shared bones (UE clip ...)")`.
  Doc comment now cites both the F13 UE montage path and the wired 1P
  viewmodel path. No exceptions, no fallback motion invented: on no-op the
  crank ring still tracks `crank_progress` (procedural HUD fallback kept).
- `_tick_wire_crank` (:1014-1032) and `_end_wire_crank` (:1035-1042):
  verified unchanged — hold on `secondary_action`, duration from
  `GameData.eval_curve("CT_WireCrank", "CrankDuration", ...)` with
  `WIRE_CRANK_DURATION_FALLBACK` (6.0 s) floor, progress published to
  `crank_progress`, charge granted on completion.
- Sustain loop verified unchanged: `_select_fp_anim_role` returns
  `"zipwire_crank"` while `_is_cranking`, and `_update_fp_anim_state`
  re-resolves it every frame via `ensure_fp_clip`, so the 1.32 s loop
  sustains for the whole crank hold.

